  "content": {
    "title": "Houston Rockets vs. Los Angeles Lakers: Stream, lineups, injury reports, broadcast (3/18)",
    "text": "March 18, 2026, 1:51 p.m. CTThe Houston Rockets will play host to the Los Angeles Lakers at their home arena of Toyota Center this Wednesday (March 18) evening. There, the Rockets will be looking to get some revenge on the Lakers after dropping the first of two tilts with Los Angeles in their home-and-home series with their Western Conference opponent.The Lakers, of course, will be trying to keep their current win streak alive with a second road win vs. Houston. With a key player likely back in the fold for the Rockets, we expect a Houston win, but this game could be closer than many expect.Records, standing, and streaksAt present, the Rockets have a 41-26 record, which has them fourth in the Western Conference standings.The Lakers are the owners of a 43-25 record and a six game win streak, good enough for third in the West.What happened in the last game for each team?Houston lost to the Lakers 100-92 at home.This was Los Angeles' last game as well.InjuriesFor Houston, Fred VanVleet (ACL), Jae'Sean Tate (knee), and Steven Adams (ankle) are out.For Los Angeles, Maxi Kleber (back) is out.Probable starting lineups - HoustonKevin DurantJabari Smith Jr.Tari EasonAlperen SengunAmen ThompsonProbable starting lineups - Los AngelesLeBron JamesDeandre AytonMarcus SmartLuka DoncicAustin ReavesWhat time is tipoff, and on what channels?Here's when you should tune in to see the game:Date: 3/18Time: 8:30 p.m. ETTV Channel: ESPNLive Stream: Fubo (watch for free)",
